prompt='''Use case: precise-object-edit. Produce one opaque native 1254x1254 square. Edit image1 at identical close-up framing and scale. Rebuild the ENTIRE broad pale-stone wall panel, its single narrow lower bevel, base plinth and floor-contact shadow as ONE continuous straight perspective object, matching the correct right-side native anchor.
CRITICAL GEOMETRY: the old long diagonal bevel on the LEFT is at the WRONG HEIGHT. Do NOT preserve its left endpoint or simply smooth it into the right endpoint. Lower and reproject the entire bevel all the way to the left edge. The correct dark fine bevel runs approximately through image pixel (0,212), (500,374), (1024,542), (1139,579), (1253,616). Use that single straight perspective line, with the narrow pale highlight immediately below it. The whole wall base and contact shadow must follow that new line. Erase the old line entirely; no second bevel, no step, no kink, no source boundary. The wall panel becomes taller on the left. The next unpainted tile to the left will follow this NEW height, so no left-edge lock applies. Do not retain the old incorrect left line near y100.
The last RIGHT230 pixels contain the CORRECT wall endpoint and perspective slope; join it exactly. Keep the foreground gold-red scroll at the far-right edge unchanged and complete. Keep the true BOTTOM230 existing paving and lower-left yellow-flowered tree at the same coordinates. Rebuild the adjacent upper paving to meet the new wall base naturally, while its stone-grid joins continue into the right and bottom anchors. The broad upper stone panel remains a close-up; its TOP COPING is outside the image. Do not zoom out, show a wall top, add a pillar, finial, divider, rail, new plants or any new object. Preserve the existing faint top-right diagonal stone seam.
Image2 supplies only the full-map arrangement, image3 material, image4 approved Q Daoist style. Bright daylight, clean crisp painted natural pale stone, restrained fine brush texture. Same exact camera, object size and crop as image1. No blur, scratches, UI, labels, text, people or comparison panel. One continuous native scene.'''
pf=R/'prompts'/f'{pid}_{ver}.prompt.txt';rf=R/'prompts'/f'{pid}_{ver}.request.json';assert not pf.exists();pf.write_text(prompt,encoding='utf-8');wr(rf,{'createdAt':datetime.now(timezone.utc).isoformat(),'promptPath':str(pf),'promptSha256':sh(pf),'references':refs,'transparent_background':False,'submittedParameters':{'model':None,'quality':None},'actualModel':None,'actualQuality':None,'coordinate':g['coordinate'],'status':'prepared_not_submitted','repairAuthority':'Parent approved complete wall lower bevel/base/shadow reconstruction on 2026-10-11; left neighbor remains ungenerated.'})
p=R/'progress-r08_c11.json';d=rd(p);d.update({'status':'submitting_complete_wall_projection_repair','currentPatch':pid+'_'+ver,'inFlight':True});wr(p,d)
print(json.dumps({'prompt':prompt,'referenced_image_paths':[r['file'] for r in refs],'transparent_background':False}))
